6. Interface & Data Architecture
Project: MESA — Mission Enterprise Services Architecture  
Artifact: MESA-IFD-001 | Status: Proposed conceptual baseline — review required  
Related artifacts: Executive Overview · CONOPS · Trade Study · Requirements · Logical Architecture · Behavioral Architecture
> **Portfolio disclaimer:** MESA is a fictional, unclassified reference architecture. All interfaces, schemas, event topics, roles, thresholds, and identifiers below are illustrative engineering examples—not descriptions of operational government or employer systems. This document uses Mermaid to depict conceptual interfaces; these are **not formal SysML IBDs** until modeled and validated in a SysML tool.
6.1 Enterprise Internal Block Diagram — IBD-001
Purpose and boundary
MESA integrates independently governed collection sources, shared enterprise services, mission applications, and reporting capabilities. The MESA integration boundary governs published contracts, authorization, metadata semantics, and event exchange; it does not prescribe constituent systems' internal implementations.
