Minimum contract fields
Each interface specification should include: `interface_id`, owner, producer, consumer, purpose, message/operation name, schema version, transport/protocol, data classification/marking profile, identity/authentication, authorization policy, latency/throughput target, delivery semantics, error codes, retry and retention policies, observability fields, test cases, and change/compatibility policy.
Sample synchronous API contract (illustrative)
```yaml
interface_id: IF-009
operation: POST /v1/workflows
caller: mission-application
owner: workflow-service
request:
  workflow_template_id: analytical-review-v1
  input_asset_ids: [asset-example-001]
  correlation_id: corr-example-001
response:
  status_code: 202
  workflow_id: wf-example-001
  state: accepted
security:
  authentication: approved-user-or-workload-identity
  authorization: workflow-submit-policy
failure_contract:
  400: invalid-request
  403: not-authorized
  409: duplicate-or-conflicting-request
  503: temporarily-unavailable
```
6.6 Common Information Model — DAT-001
Information entities
Entity	Core fields	Purpose
SourceSystem	`source_system_id`, `owner`, `interface_version`	Identify independently managed producer
Observation	`observation_id`, `source_system_id`, `observed_at`, `received_at`, `marking`, `schema_version`	Represent source-originated information
DataAsset	`asset_id`, `object_uri`, `content_hash`, `media_type`, `registered_at`, `marking`	Link stored object to catalog record
ProcessingActivity	`activity_id`, `input_asset_ids`, `processor_version`, `started_at`, `completed_at`, `output_asset_ids`	Record transformation lineage
WorkflowExecution	`workflow_id`, `template_version`, `state`, `correlation_id`, `initiator_id`	Track mission processing
AnalyticalResult	`result_id`, `workflow_id`, `source_asset_ids`, `output_asset_id`	Associate outputs with source evidence
ReportProduct	`report_id`, `version`, `approval_state`, `approved_by`, `released_at`	Govern reporting and dissemination
Canonical metadata example
```json
{
  "asset_id": "asset-example-001",
  "source_system_id": "source-example-a",
  "observation_id": "obs-example-001",
  "observed_at": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z",
  "received_at": "2026-10-20T14:00:05Z",
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "media_type": "application/octet-stream",
  "object_uri": "mesa://objects/asset-example-001",
  "content_hash": "sha256:EXAMPLE_REPLACE_WITH_VALID_DIGEST",
  "marking": "SYNTHETIC-DEMO",
  "correlation_id": "corr-example-001",
  "provenance_activity_id": "activity-example-001"
}
```
Validation rules: IDs must be unique within their defined namespace; timestamps use ISO 8601 with offsets; source and marking fields are mandatory; schema version must be recognized; object references are resolved only after authorization. The `SYNTHETIC-DEMO` marking is a placeholder, not an official classification or dissemination marking.
Semantic and governance rules
Preserve source identifiers and observation time separately from ingestion time.
Use approved enterprise vocabulary and unit conventions; retain source values for audit where required.
Distinguish immutable source evidence from derived or transformed assets.
Version schemas and transformations; document compatibility rules.
Maintain a provenance link for every derived output, including failed or partial processing when required.
Apply authorization to metadata visibility as well as object retrieval.
6.7 Event Topics, Schemas & Data Lineage
Proposed event topic catalog
Topic	Publisher	Subscriber(s)	Payload emphasis	Delivery consideration
`collection.observation.available.v1`	Source adapter	Ingestion workers	Observation ID, object reference	Duplicate-safe; replayable
`ingestion.asset.validated.v1`	Validation service	Storage/registration workflow	Validation outcome, canonical asset	Ordered by asset only if required
`catalog.asset.registered.v1`	Catalog service	Workflow engine, search indexer	Catalog ID, asset ID	Publish after authoritative commit
`workflow.execution.started.v1`	Workflow engine	Operations / provenance	Workflow ID, initiator context	Audit and correlation
`workflow.task.completed.v1`	Task adapter	Workflow engine	Task ID, outcome, result reference	Idempotent completion processing
`analytics.result.available.v1`	Analytics service	Workflow/report service	Result ID, provenance reference	Data access separately authorized
`report.product.approved.v1`	Report approval service	Dissemination service	Report ID, approval reference	Do not bypass release policy
`configuration.baseline.approved.v1`	CM service	Architecture analytics	Baseline ID, version	Authenticated governance event
